SUMMARY:CBH Talk | Forgotten History: The Brooklyn Theater Fire of 1876
LOCATION:Brooklyn Public Library
DESCRIPTION:On December 5\, 1876\, a fire broke out during a performance at
 
 the Brooklyn Theatre\, then one of the city’s most prominent playhouses.
 
 Within half an hour\, the theater was destroyed and nearly 300 people had 
 
perished\, making the Brooklyn Theatre fire one of the deadliest disasters 
 
in New York City hi Tickets & info: https://www.bklynlibrary.org/calendar/c
 
bh-talk-forgotten-center-for-brooklyn-20261203-0630pm
